      "type": "ziak-feature-story",
      "blocks": {
        "t1": { "type": "text", "settings": { "text": "<p>A ZIAK shoe doesn't begin on a factory line — it begins with a decision to do things properly. Every pair passes through many pairs of hands before it reaches yours, and each set of hands leaves something behind: precision, patience, and a little pride.</p>" } },
        "h1": { "type": "heading", "settings": { "text": "It Starts with the Leather" } },
        "duo1": { "type": "duo", "settings": { "layout": "image_left", "subheading": "Choosing the hide", "text": "<p>Before a single cut is made, the leather is chosen by hand. We look for full-grain hides with an even surface and a natural pull-up — leather that will soften and deepen in colour as you wear it, rather than crack or fade.</p>", "ph_label": "Add leather / material photo" } },
        "h2": { "type": "heading", "settings": { "text": "Cutting &amp; Clicking" } },
        "t2": { "type": "text", "settings": { "text": "<p>The pattern is laid out and every panel is cut — a stage traditionally called \"clicking\" for the sound the blade makes. It's here that a maker's eye matters most: aligning the grain, avoiding blemishes, and making sure the two shoes of a pair will look like true twins.</p>" } },
        "vid": { "type": "video", "settings": { "ph_label": "Add shoemaking video", "caption": "Inside the workshop — from cut to finished last." } },
        "h3": { "type": "heading", "settings": { "text": "Lasting the Shoe" } },
        "duo2": { "type": "duo", "settings": { "layout": "image_right", "subheading": "Shaping over the last", "text": "<p>The upper is stretched and moulded over a wooden or resin form called a last — the mould that gives the shoe its shape and fit. This is where a flat piece of leather becomes something with posture and character.</p>", "ph_label": "Add lasting / shaping photo" } },
        "q1": { "type": "quote", "settings": { "text": "Machines can be fast. Only a craftsperson can be careful.", "cite": "The ZIAK Workshop" } },
        "h4": { "type": "heading", "settings": { "text": "The Finishing Touch" } },
        "t3": { "type": "text", "settings": { "text": "<p>Soles are attached, edges are trimmed and burnished, and the leather is polished by hand until it holds a quiet shine. The result isn't just a shoe — it's the sum of dozens of small, deliberate choices, made so you never have to think about them.</p>" } },
